+    // already sign-extended into bits [63:32]. A non-overflow cast that only sign-extends a
+    // 32-bit value -- int->int (same size) or signed int->long widening -- is therefore a pure
+    // no-op when its operand is produced by such a W-form op. RyuJIT still emits it as a
+    // `sext.w`; because the cast gets its own destination register the emit-level peephole can
+    // at best turn it into a `mv`, not delete it. Removing the GT_CAST node here, before LSRA,
+    // drops the operation AND the redundant register/move: the consumer reads the operand's
+    // already-sign-extended 64-bit register directly. The parent selects its W/non-W form from
+    // its own type, so feeding it the TYP_INT operand is value-correct (a spilled TYP_INT temp
+    // reloads with a sign-extending `lw`).
